Thank you for your submission. After reviewing your report, this issue has been previously reported and assessed in report #3537798. Both reports describe a command injection vulnerability in the Vercel CLI MCP command where unsanitized user input in the --project-name parameter is passed to execSync(), allowing arbitrary command execution through shell metacharacters.
The original report identified the same vulnerable file (packages/cli/src/commands/mcp/mcp.ts), the same vulnerable code lines in both Cursor and VS Code integrations, and demonstrated the identical attack vector using malicious project names to break out of the command context.
Since this vulnerability instance has already been reported and is being tracked under the original submission, this report is being closed as a duplicate.
